  "answer_for_xiao_man": "On T4, fixed_matched catch=100%, fail_escalate=22% (cross-field miss 22/31), schema_cap=100%. Cheap pre-check that deepens only on P1/P2 fail misses the cross-field population — those artifacts pass shallow probes, so the cascade never fires. Cascade is fine if the ceiling is schema-matched depth (continue on pass up to Pi), not failure-signal-driven. fail_escalate looks cheaper (7.1 vs 29.8 ops) — that is the trap, not the win. Answer: P-level is fixed by task/schema type in this setup; dynamic deepen-on-fail is not a substitute for matched depth. Fixture + instrumented ops, same caveats as dual-axis."
